    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphlăgo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> ), ŏnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παφλαγών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Paphlagonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphlagonum sata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Avien. Perieg. 969</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Curt. 6, 11, 4</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 3,
			72</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphlă-gŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Paphlagonian</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 2, 2, §
				5</span></i>.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphlăgŏnĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the province of
				Paphlagonia</i>, <i>between Bithynia and
			Pontus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 1, 2, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 19, 8</span></i>.</div>
